From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:50:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: rockchip: vpu2: decode MPEG-4 Part 2,
 H.263 and Sorenson Spark

The VDPU2 decoder decodes MPEG-4 Part 2 (decoding mode 1) and H.263
(mode 2), which with the Sorenson escape coding enabled also covers
Sorenson Spark. Add them on the stateless MPEG-4 and H.263 controls, as
the V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_SLICE, V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263_SLICE and
V4L2_PIX_FMT_SPK_SLICE coded formats of the VDPU2 variants (RK3328,
RK3399, RK3568, RK3588 VPU121 and PX30), so that applications find out
from VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT which decoders can decode them. The resolution is
limited to 1920x1088 like the other VDPU2 codecs.

The hardware parses the macroblock layer of a whole VOP or picture,
video packet and GOB headers included, so one job decodes one OUTPUT
buffer and the optional slice parameter controls are not used. It starts
from a 64-bit aligned address with a bit offset, given by the
data_bit_offset of the VOP or picture control.

B-VOPs need the motion vectors of the co-located macroblocks of their
backward reference for the direct mode. P-VOPs write them, 16 bytes per
macroblock, after the picture in their capture buffer, which is grown
for MPEG-4 like for H.264; B-VOPs read them from the backward reference
buffer, and are told by the coding type of that reference whether it
has any. The TRB / TRD ratios of the frame and field direct modes are
programmed as 27-bit fractions.

The quantisation matrices are loaded in raster order, the order the
MPEG-2 mode of the same decoder uses. The encoder quirk which the
hardware reproduces is the extension of the reference VOPs from their
exact size instead of the macroblock aligned one (DivX 4), which is
advertised through the maximum of V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_QUIRKS.

The hardware has no global motion compensation, no data partitioning and
no reversible VLC, and decodes baseline H.263 only: the controls which
need them are refused.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
